he\n * language tokenizers, sets up web workers, and emits the `monaco-colors`\n * style tag with `.mtk*` token-color rules ‚Äî none of which happens when you\n * `import \&#39;monaco-editor\&#39;` directly with a raw webpack setup.\n *\n * wp-scripts loads this file for every `npm run build:scripts:*`&#39;..., &#39;content_hash&#39; =&gt; &#39;58afd47c9f0ebea8d3318d11875ed20df7bd8fef393d385a03117a527bc12e41&#39;, &#39;created_at&#39; =&gt; &#39;2026-04-10 23:13:36&#39;, &#39;updated_at&#39; =&gt; &#39;2026-04-10 23:13:36&#39;], 1 =&gt; [&#39;id&#39; =&gt; &#39;13&#39;, &#39;lagoon_id&#39; =&gt; &#39;62&#39;, &#39;owner_id&#39; =&gt; &#39;1&#39;, &#39;visibility&#39; =&gt; &#39;public&#39;, &#39;file_order&#39; =&gt; &#39;1&#39;, &#39;name&#39; =&gt; &#39;untitled.txt&#39;, &#39;description&#39; =&gt; &#39;&#39;, &#39;language&#39; =&gt; &#39;markdown&#39;, &#39;content&#39; =&gt; &#39;# Kitchen Sink Markdown\n\nA test snippet exercising **GitHub Flavoured Markdown** features so we can verify rendering and styling end-to-end.\n\n## Inline formatting\n\nPlain, **bold**, *italic*, ***bold italic***, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and a [link to nowhere](https://example.com &quot;tooltip text&quot;).\n\nAuto-linked URL: https://codelagoon.gq\n\nFootnote reference[^1] and another[^note].\n\n[^1]: This is the first footnote.\n[^note]: Footnotes can have **markdown** in them too.\n\n---\n\n## Headings\n\n# H1\n## H2\n### &#39;..., &#39;content_hash&#39; =&gt; &#39;c8fd1be43f7cec9a3bb735b2c9e544ebf3d582ea53d87db9eaa046b98e4189c9&#39;, &#39;created_at&#39; =&gt; &#39;2026-04-10 23:13:36&#39;, &#39;updated_at&#39; =&gt; &#39;2026-04-10 23:13:36&#39;]]</span> )</td><td title='/shared/httpd/CodeLagoon/htdocs/wp-content/mu-plugins/codelag-features/src/Download/ZipDownloadHandler.php' bgcolor='#eeeeec'>.../ZipDownloadHandler.php<b>:</b>96</td></tr>
